From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:44:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 85/91] web-app: rounded waveform bars, smooth progress, RMS
 peaks

Loud voice messages drew as solid blocks: bucketPeaks kept the loudest
sample per bucket (max-abs), and a phone mic with automatic gain touches
full scale in almost every bucket, so nearly every bar hit full height. It
now takes RMS per bucket (perceived loudness) and normalizes to the
recording's own 95th percentile, so quiet messages fill the height too. The
reference is floored at a quarter of the loudest bucket: when speech fills
<5% of the buckets, p95 is the mic's background noise and would otherwise
draw the noise at full height.

drawBars draws rounded 3px pills at a fixed 5px pitch: the bar count follows
the canvas width (the 128 source peaks, up from 64, are averaged down to
fit), so bars look the same in a narrow phone bubble and a wide desktop one,
and silence still draws a 3px dot. The played/unplayed split is a clip at
the exact progress x, so the accent colour sweeps through a bar instead of
flipping a whole bar at a time (one of the old 64 bars covered ~3s of a
3-minute message). The recorder's live meter shares drawBars and gets the
same look.

ponytail: progress still updates on `timeupdate` (~4 Hz), not every frame;
add a rAF loop while playing if the sweep looks steppy.
